# Design & UX Planning Rule

Do not jump straight to implementation. Before writing UI for a feature or bug
fix, plan the **design** and **usability** for **web and mobile**. Compose
shadcn primitives only — see [docs/DESIGN_DOC.md](../../docs/DESIGN_DOC.md) §6.

## Plan first (required)

Write a short plan covering:

1. **Job to be done** — what the user is trying to finish on this screen.
2. **Surfaces** — which routes/pages share the state (list, detail, favorites, chrome).
3. **States** — default, loading, empty, error, filtered/search, one-item, overflow.
4. **Breakpoints** — mobile (~375px) and desktop (~1280px). Tablet follows the closer of the two.
5. **Input** — touch (44px targets, no hover-only actions) and pointer/keyboard.

If the plan is missing a mobile or desktop path, stop and complete it before coding.

## Layout

| Viewport | Expectation |
| -------- | ----------- |
| Mobile | Single column. Primary action reachable with the thumb. Search + filter stack; they do not sit in one cramped row. Nav stays usable (wrap or compact header). Cards are full-width with readable type. |
| Desktop | Use width for a card grid and side-by-side search/filter. Do not hide mobile-only flows — same tasks must be possible. |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hover-only favorite; filter row overflows on 375px
<div className="flex items-center gap-4">
  <Input className="w-80" />
  <Select />
  <button className="opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100">♥</button>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — stack on small screens; always-visible control
<div className="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-end">
  <Input aria-label="Search shows" />
  <Select /* status filter */ />
</div>
<Button variant="ghost" size="icon" aria-label="Add to favorites" />
```

## Usability checklist

- Same tasks work on both viewports (browse, search, filter, open detail, favorite).
- Loading / empty / error are distinct and not color-only.
- Images have alt text; controls have accessible names.
- Infinite lists do not trap keyboard or hide the header.
- Do not recreate Button, Card, Input, Select, or Dropdown Menu.

## Verify

Exercise the flow on **desktop and a ~375px viewport** (browser tools or the
closest substitute). A single desktop screenshot is not done.
